# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Batatia, Benner, Chiang, ..., Csanyi (2024). A foundation model for
#   atomistic materials chemistry. arXiv:2401.00096
#   (also published as the MACE-MP-0 paper).
#
# Encoding scope: MACE-MP-0 (specifically the MACE-MP-0b3 medium-sized
# release), an equivariant message-passing foundation model trained on
# the MPtrj dataset and used out-of-the-box across a wide diversity of
# chemical systems. As with chen2022 and deng2023, this is a universal /
# foundation potential; we encode the coverage as a single
# MaterialSystem (mat-MP-universal-batatia2024mp0) and document the
# protocol limitation in Q12.

@prefix rdf:    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:    <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit:   <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips:  <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix ex:     <https://example.org/mlips/kg/> .

###############################################################################
# Q1 -- Bibliographic identification
###############################################################################

